        "body": "A useful sample includes a routine close, a reopened case, a missing document index, and a handoff that crossed a shift. Report open cases by age and dependency, not only the total, because a stable total can hide an aging tail. If the gap is caused by a missing document index, simplify the collection step or move it earlier in the workflow. Track the number of sampled cases, the number with missing evidence, and the number reopened after review.\n\nInclude a case where the owner said no or asked for more evidence; those decisions show whether the boundary is working. Compare document index completeness before and after a process change, using the same definitions and observation window. When the same gap appears twice, change the intake field, the approval rule, or the conflict database permission instead of repeating the coaching. Review at least one case handled by a backup owner and one that crossed a time zone."
